        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.41,
            0.887,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sequence of heights forms a GP with a = 18 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "r = 0.75"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , that is, 18, 13.5, 10.125, 7.594, 5.695, 4.27125, 3.2034375, … . We see that after the seventh bounce the ball remains below "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{6}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the height at which it started."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.371,
            0.539,
            0.624,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 8.3"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.591,
            0.886,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term of a GP with common ratio 2, whose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "8 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term is 192."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.634,
            0.722,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " terms of the GP: 5, 25, 125, … ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.658,
            0.885,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*3. A sequence is given by the recursive rule "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t_{1} = 2, t_{n + 1} = 3t_{n} - 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Which term of the sequence is 730?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.701,
            0.886,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Which term of the GP: 2, 6, 18, … is 4374? Write the explicit formula as well as the recursive formula for the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.743,
            0.887,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. A ball is dropped from a height of 80 metres. After hitting the ground, it bounces back to 60% of the height from which it fell. It continues bouncing in this way — each time rising to 60% of the previous height."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.826,
            0.804,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What height does the ball reach after the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " bounce?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.852,
            0.886,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What is the total vertical distance the ball has travelled by the time it hits the ground for the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " time?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
